        "original_id": "453ac258-45ff-500e-97f2-d41a1a065496",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Sheridan County, Montana; Chandra Taal; Plentywood\n- Products: Sher-Wood Airport\n- Topics: Montana; Himachal Pradesh; Lahul and Spiti district; Spiti\n\nFacts:\n- Sheridan County is a county in the U.S. state of Montana.\n- Chandra Taal, also called Chandra Tal and meaning \"Lake of the Moon,\" is in the Spiti area of Lahul and Spiti district in Himachal Pradesh, India.\n- Sher-Wood Airport is a public-use airport located one nautical mile northeast of the central business district of Plentywood in Sheridan County, Montana, United States.\n- Sher-Wood Airport has the codes IATA PWD, ICAO KPWD, and FAA LID PWD.",
